Z||000028||frontal lobe||11-02-2001||01:04 AM||||Aspirin overdose will kill you FASTER than ibuprofen overdose, for those in a hurry I guess.  Maybe by a day, two at the most.  So a hundred years from now, you would have been dead .005% longer.<P>Ibuprofen would be considered somewhat safer over-all than aspirin.  Somewhat less ulcer risk, and somewhat larger safety margin based on larger difference between recommended dose and lethal dose.||||reg||1
Z||000029||RossT||11-02-2001||01:33 AM||||I should check the ot section more often!!<P>Ok, Your max. 24 hour intake of tyenol should be LESS than 4,000 mg!!!!!!  Take no more than that!  If you have been drinking, do not take tylenol to help a hangover.<P>So for extra strenght tylenol 500mg, take no more than 8 per day.  If you are taking prescription pain killers such as Darvocet N-100 or Lorcet 10/650, you can have up to 6 of these a day. 6X650 is &lt;4,000 mg.<P>I personally never take tylenol.  Hate the stuff.  I see several OD's every week..<P>Frontal, This weekend its my turn to do the radio thing!!  finally got a daily driver fiero!!  Thanks for being the test subject for me..<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||1
