Z||000031||Ken Wittlief||11-02-2001||11:43 AM||||A paramedic told me once the WORST thing that people do to commit suicide is drink Drano or a similar lye based product.<P> It disolves your stomach, then proceeds to disolve everything else in your abdomin. He said by the time the parametics arrive there is nothing they can do to stop you from dying - and its one of the most painfull ways to go.<P> In fact, I think he said even if you change your mind right away at try to throw the stuff back up, its still to late.<P> Personally I never understood why someone who wants to die often does it in a fashion that is extreemly painful and, well, destructive. I guess they are punishing themselves in some way - but then again I never understood why someone would want to kill themselves in the first place, unless they are terminally ill. <P> People who are executed by lethal injection die a much more quick and painless death than most people that commit suicide - I guess the bottom line is the latter are simply not thinking clearly. ||||reg||11
Z||000032||Ken Wittlief||11-02-2001||11:54 AM||||On a lighter note - a friend of mine was a marine, and in bootcamp there was a guy who would eat stuff for money<P> I dont know how it got started - at dinner someone spit out a piece of grizzel from a steak and complained about the food, and the guy picked it up and said, "theres nothing wrong with this meat" and swallowed it.<P> after a couple weeks of this kinda stuff someone dared him to drink a small bottle of Wisk - a collection was taken up and they had about $50 that people had pitched in to see him do it.<P> The guy was ready to drink the stuff, and noticed the posion control statement on the back of the bottle - so he thought maybe he better call them first to see what the stuff would do to him.<P> So they all crowd around a pay phone and the guy calls the poison contol hotline and asks "What would happen to you if you drank a 16 oz bottle of Wisk?"<P> and the lady on the other end freaks out! "OH my GOD! Where are you? I'll get an ambulance dispatched to you immediatly - just give me your address!"<P> and he tells her, "I didnt drink it yet................ I was just thinking about it!"||||reg||10
Z||000033||frontal lobe||11-02-2001||12:42 PM||||STOP THE INSANITY!<P>If you drink lye or acid, it WILL burn up your esophagus.  So even if you vomited it out of your stomach before it damaged the stomach (which has a much tougher lining), you are still out of luck.  A HORRIBLE way to die.||||reg||1
Z||000034||DaRkLoRD||11-02-2001||03:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Could you be feeling more tension from this job without realizing it?Is it possible that those lights are acting like a strobe and contributing to your problem?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I feel a LOT of tension from my job.. not the least of which is they offered me a certain salary, but when I took the job, they cut it in half, got rid of ALL the benefits, and have me doing a lot more than I was hired for.. (was even way up on a ladder running network cables, and I have no insurance, not covered under workers comp. and I've had no fall protection safety training..) and plus, I haven't been paid in 3 weeks now, and they always joke about how I make so much money etc. that I should buy them beer after work.. (I make $7.50/hr US)<P>but.. there aren't any other jobs around here. I've been looking...<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||11
