Z||000037||Matthew_Fiero||11-02-2001||06:36 PM||||eww drano! that would be quite painful. You would think if you were suicidal you would think something better than that. Come to think of it, what would the the quickest way?<BR>obviously jumping off a cliff or hanging yourself, i dunno. But to eat something. Maybe sucking on a lead bullet for a day<BR>haha ||||reg||1
Z||000038||Ken Wittlief||11-03-2001||01:20 AM||||The thing that bothers me about suicide is when someones heart stops, or they stop breathing, you can bring them back after several minutes and they can fully recover.<P> so even though their heart was not beating, they were still alive.<P> so I wonder - how long after their heart stopped were they still conscience?!<P> if you shoot yourself in the chest, how long does your brain stay alive, and maybe conscience, now in incredible pain.<P> And how do you know if you leap off a high building and splatter yourself - how do you know your brain will not stay 'online' for several minutes until it finally dies from oxygen starvation?!<P> But the real question is, if you kill yourself, how do you know you wont end up 'somewhere' or in some situation that is a thousand times worse than where you are now? Im not talking about religious ideas or hell or anything. If you continue to exist after death then you have at least a 50:50 chance that things might be worse after you are dead than they are now.<P> as long as you are alive you can explore other options and change your mind. But once you are dead there is no going back.||||reg||11
Z||000039||frontal lobe||11-03-2001||02:18 AM||||Usually after 4 seconds of no heartbeat, a person starts to lose consciousness and faint.  So shoot yourself in the chest--you may be conscious for a few seconds, but losing consciousness during those seconds.  Brain pretty much irreversibly damaged after 4 minutes.<P>Regarding jumping out of a building, picture those wacky late night stunts where they drop watermelons off buildings.  The brain connections are going to be quite "disconnected" so that will be instantaneous.||||reg||1
