Z||000043||JSocha||11-03-2001||09:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>if you shoot yourself in the chest, how long does your brain stay alive, and maybe conscience, now in incredible pain.<P> And how do you know if you leap off a high building and splatter yourself - how do you know your brain will not stay 'online' for several minutes until it finally dies from oxygen starvation?!<P> But the real question is, if you kill yourself, how do you know you wont end up 'somewhere' or in some situation that is a thousand times worse than where you are now? Im not talking about religious ideas or hell or anything. If you continue to exist after death then you have at least a 50:50 chance that things might be worse after you are dead than they are now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've always wondered about something similar.  What about decapitation?  Is the brain still registering?  Not like your head can yell out without the lungs "Ouch that hurts!".  How do we know that the person isn't seeing things around them and the brain is registering and remembering the activity.<P>Things that make you go "hmmmmmmmm?"<P>Does make you wonder also about the 50/50 possibility.<P>Dead...in another space/time continum...one can go into the girls locker room and enjoy the scenery-Good thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ...Can't touch the goodies-Bad thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> .||||reg||1
