Z||000046||Mach10||11-04-2001||02:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Well, from what I remember, you are still "conscious" for about 20-40 seconds after being decapitated.  Anyways, Tylenol (Acetaminophen) destroys the liver and kindeys in a slow (meaning, years and years) process (jaundice, etc).. Asprin (Acetacelycitic Acid (sp?)) effects the stomach more so. Either way is not a wise way.<BR>  <BR>Frontal Lobe: You are spewing out the obvious here..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Sorry, where's your degree? Where are you getting this info? Your brain shuts down plenty fast with no blood flow... 20-30 seconds?!?<BR>Here's an example... In Hapkido, one of the choke techniques I use cut off both the air (forarm over windpipe) and drastically reduces circulation (twisting crushing motion with arm and shirt). I've had it done to me by a master, and I start greying out in under 2 seconds. I'd be flat out unconcious in 5-6. Here's the important bit: <I>even with the choke there is still bloodflow, and that blood still has a good amount of oxygen in it</I> and it takes under 10s to go unconscious... I can guarantee that it would take much less time if there is a TOTAL loss of blood pressure.<P><BR>The fastest and most irreversible way to kill yourself was demonstrated in "Dr. Strangelove..." Riding <B>The Bomb</B> out of an airplane  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000047||JohnnyK||11-04-2001||06:33 PM||||Woo.. Hugh's a little bitter. My father is a DDS, we have talked about this many a times. And I used to study this crap day in day out honestly for the fun of it years ago. As for the decapitation, you are still going for a few seconds, and can even blink.||||reg||1
Z||000048||Mach10||11-04-2001||06:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Woo.. Hugh's a little bitter. My father is a DDS, we have talked about this many a times. And I used to study this crap day in day out honestly for the fun of it years ago. As for the decapitation, you are still going for a few seconds, and can even blink.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Pretty huge gap from "a few seconds" to 20-30 seconds  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Low-level drugs like these do tend to have cumulative effects on one's system. The situation we were talking about was a massive shock dose. A few bottles of Tylenol will make lindberger cheese out of your liver in a matter of hours... <BR>Long-term effects of high (but not lethal) doses will give the symptoms you describe. Uh... Pretty much that FR has been saying for the past several posts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||12
